  # @option opts [Boolean] :detect_fields Set up the PDF's fields as DocSpring's "Automatically detect fields" upload option does: import or detect the fields, name them with AI, and set up conditional logic. `field_source`, `field_naming` and `field_logic` choose how. Default false. `document.page_processing_statuses` and `document.field_logic_status` show how it's going, and `document.state` becomes `processed` once every page's fields are set up.
  # @option opts [FieldSetupSource] :field_source With `detect_fields`, where the fields come from. `auto` (the default) imports the form fields of a fillable PDF and detects the fields of a PDF without them; `pdf_detection` detects the fields from the page layout, even on a fillable PDF; `pdf_form_fields` only imports the PDF's form fields.
  # @option opts [FieldSetupNaming] :field_naming With `detect_fields`, how the fields are named. `ai` (the default) names them and sets their types and settings with AI; `preserve` keeps the names of the PDF's form fields, and AI only names the fields it detected. `preserve` needs `field_source` `auto` or `pdf_form_fields`.
  # @option opts [FieldSetupLogic] :field_logic With `detect_fields`, whether AI reads the whole form once the fields are named and sets up conditional logic and required fields (`ai`) or not (`none`). Default: your account's template settings.
